  "info": {
    "description": "Explicit proxy to Routeware WebRW. Session cookies are stored in a Worker Durable Object; clients do not send Routeware credentials.

**Customer:** \`customers-read\` lists rows; \`detail-full\` loads one record; \`customer-types-read\` feeds dropdowns; \`add-new-long\` and \`load-long-modal\` return the same HTML/JS shells the SPA uses before save; \`save-long-form\` creates or updates (URL-encoded form body). **Anti-forgery** for \`save-long-form\` is filled server-side from Routeware modal HTML when the client omits \`__RequestVerificationToken\` (see \`CUSTOMER_SAVE_AUTO_TOKEN\`). Routeware does not support HTTP DELETE for customers — use \`save-long-form\` with \`Enabled=false\` to disable. \`DELETE /api/v1/routeware/customer\` documents that limitation (returns 405 + problem+json).

**D1 snapshots (Routeware custom CSV reports):** \`customer_snapshot\` (CustomerID) → \`address_snapshot\` (PickupAddressID, CustomerID) → \`container_snapshot\` (ContainerID, PickupAddressID). **Export source:** set \`*_REPORT_EXPORT_PATH\` (static URL) **or** \`*_REPORT_QUERY_ID\` (WebRW: client \`requestID\` + \`GET\` \`QueryExecuteDownload\`), then \`POST /api/v1/data-snapshot/sync\` (bearer) or the daily cron. \`POST /api/v1/...-snapshot/import\` accepts a raw CSV body. See \`CUSTOMER_SNAPSHOT.md\` for setup and migration commands.

**Data entity (\`/api/v1/data/*\`, tag \`data-entity\`):** bearer = \`CUSTOMER_SNAPSHOT_SYNC_SECRET\`. \`GET\` reads nested D1 snapshots (customer + address + container graph) with ETag/cache. \`POST\` applies changes to Routeware, returns ids + sync outcome only (never submitted fields or the upstream body), then refreshes D1 from \`GetCustomerDetailFull\` and invalidates that cache for affected ids.",
    "title": "Routeware Shadow API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
  },
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "paths": {
    "/api/v1/address-snapshot": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Routeware addresses (\`PickupAddressID\` → \`CustomerID\`). Optional filters: \`customerId\`, \`pickupAddressId\`, free-text on street \`q\`, \`enabled\`. Pass \`cursor\` (the previous page's \`nextCursor\`) instead of \`offset\` to page deep result sets by primary-key seek instead of a scanned OFFSET.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "customerId",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "example": 345734,
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null",
              ],
            },
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "pickupAddressId",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "example": 10,
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null",
              ],
            },
          },
          {
            "description": "Address line substring (case-insensitive; maximum 100 Unicode code points)",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "q",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "description": "Address line substring (case-insensitive; maximum 100 Unicode code points)",
              "example": "Main",
              "maxLength": 100,
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "enabled",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "default": "any",
              "enum": [
                "true",
                "false",
                "any",
              ],
              "example": "true",
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "limit",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "default": 50,
              "example": 50,
              "maximum": 500,
              "minimum": 1,
              "type": "integer",
            },
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "offset",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "default": 0,
              "example": 0,
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null",
              ],
            },
          },
          {
            "description": "Last pickup_address_id from the previous page's nextCursor; takes precedence over offset",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "cursor",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "description": "Last pickup_address_id from the previous page's nextCursor; takes precedence over offset",
              "example": 9,
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null",
              ],
            },
          },
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "nextCursor": null,
                  "rows": [
                    {
                      "address": "1 Main St",
                      "city": "Example City",
                      "comments": null,
                      "customer_id": 345734,
                      "driver_note": null,
                      "enabled": 1,
                      "extras_allowed": 0,
                      "franchise_id": "1",
                      "last_audit_date": null,
                      "latitude": null,
                      "longitude": null,
                      "pickup_address_id": 10,
                      "route_id": 1,
                      "state": "TX",
                      "synced_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
                      "zip": "76541",
                    },
                  ],
                  "total": 1,
                },
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CustomerSnapshotList",
                },
              },
            },
            "description": "Rows and total",
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Invalid query (application/problem+json). The zod validator rejects \`q\` longer than 100 Unicode code points, an out-of-range \`limit\`/\`offset\`, or an unknown \`enabled\` value before any D1 query runs.",
          },
        },
        "summary": "List address snapshot rows (D1)",
        "tags": [
          "address-snapshot",
        ],
      },
    },
    "/api/v1/address-snapshot/export": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Streams every \`address_snapshot\` row as CSV (\`Content-Disposition: attachment\`, filename \`address-snapshot.csv\`) in \`pickup_address_id\` order. Reads in keyset pages so a full-table export never buffers the table in memory. Emits a content-hash \`ETag\`; replay it as \`If-None-Match\` for a \`304\` with an empty body. Requires \`Authorization: Bearer <CUSTOMER_SNAPSHOT_SYNC_SECRET>\`.",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "text/csv": {
                "example": "PickupAddressID,CustomerID,RouteID,Address,City,State,Zip,FranchiseID,Comments,ExtrasAllowed,Enabled,DriverNote,Latitude,Longitude,Last_Audit_Date,_shadow_csv_encoding,synced_at
10,345734,1,1 Main St,Example City,TX,76541,1,,false,true,,,,,1,2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z
",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
            },
            "description": "CSV download (header line plus one line per row)",
          },
          "304": {
            "description": "Not modified (If-None-Match carries the current ETag)",
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthorized",
          },
        },
        "summary": "Download address snapshot as CSV",
        "tags": [
          "address-snapshot",
        ],
      },
    },
    "/api/v1/address-snapshot/import": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Raw CSV (Routeware Address Details custom report); \`Content-Type: text/csv\` or \`application/octet-stream\`. Bear the same secret; import **customers** first to satisfy \`customer_id\` foreign keys. Pass \`?dryRun=true\` to validate and return the would-be counts without writing D1.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "description": "Dry run: validate the CSV and return the would-be counts without writing D1 or R2",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "dryRun",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "description": "Dry run: validate the CSV and return the would-be counts without writing D1 or R2",
              "enum": [
                "true",
                "false",
              ],
              "example": "true",
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/octet-stream": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "string",
              },
            },
            "text/csv": {
              "example": "PickupAddressID,CustomerID,RouteID,Address,City,State,Zip,FranchiseID,Comments,ExtrasAllowed,Enabled,DriverNote,Latitude,Longitude,Last_Audit_Date
10,5,,1 Main St,Killeen,TX,76541,,,false,true,,,,",
              "schema": {
                "type": "string",
              },
            },
          },
          "description": "Routeware Address Details CSV (header + data rows — see example)",
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "deleted": 0,
                  "rowCount": 2,
                  "upserted": 2,
                },
                "schema": {
                  "properties": {
                    "deleted": {
                      "type": "integer",
                    },
                    "rowCount": {
                      "type": "integer",
                    },
                    "upserted": {
                      "type": "integer",
                    },
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "upserted",
                    "rowCount",
                  ],
                  "type": "object",
                },
              },
            },
            "description": "Result",
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Empty body (application/problem+json). Returned when the POST has no request body; post the CSV as raw body.",
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthorized",
          },
          "415": {
            "description": "Unsupported Content-Type (application/problem+json)",
          },
        },
        "summary": "Import address CSV body into D1",
        "tags": [
          "address-snapshot",
        ],
      },
    },
    "/api/v1/address-snapshot/sync": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Same bearer as \`customer-snapshot\` sync. Requires \`ADDRESS_REPORT_EXPORT_PATH\` or \`ADDRESS_REPORT_QUERY_ID\`. Customers should exist in D1 (run customer import/sync first) so \`customer_id\` foreign keys are satisfied. Pass \`?dryRun=true\` to run the full parse/validate path, return the counts that WOULD apply, and write nothing (no D1, no R2).",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "description": "Dry run: validate the CSV and return the would-be counts without writing D1 or R2",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "dryRun",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "description": "Dry run: validate the CSV and return the would-be counts without writing D1 or R2",
              "enum": [
                "true",
                "false",
              ],
              "example": "true",
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "deleted": 0,
                  "rowCount": 2,
                  "upserted": 2,
                },
                "schema": {
                  "properties": {
                    "deleted": {
                      "type": "integer",
                    },
                    "rowCount": {
                      "type": "integer",
                    },
                    "skipped": {
                      "type": "boolean",
                    },
                    "upserted": {
                      "type": "integer",
                    },
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "upserted",
                    "rowCount",
                  ],
                  "type": "object",
                },
              },
            },
            "description": "Result",
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthorized",
          },
          "503": {
            "description": "Service Unavailable",
          },
        },
        "summary": "Fetch address report CSV and upsert D1",
        "tags": [
          "address-snapshot",
        ],
      },
    },
    "/api/v1/address-snapshot/{pickupAddressId}": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Reads one row from the daily snapshot DB by \`pickupAddressId\`. Bearer-gated like every \`/api/v1/*\` route except \`GET /api/v1/health\`. Returns 404 when no row exists for that id.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "pickupAddressId",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "example": 10,
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null",
              ],
            },
          },
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "address": "1 Main St",
                  "city": "Example City",
                  "comments": null,
                  "customer_id": 345734,
                  "driver_note": null,
                  "enabled": 1,
                  "extras_allowed": 0,
                  "franchise_id": "1",
                  "last_audit_date": null,
                  "latitude": null,
                  "longitude": null,
                  "pickup_address_id": 10,
                  "route_id": 1,
                  "state": "TX",
                  "synced_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
                  "zip": "76541",
                },
                "schema": {
                  "additionalProperties": {},
                  "type": "object",
                },
              },
            },
            "description": "Row",
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Invalid id (application/problem+json)",
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found (application/problem+json)",
          },
        },
        "summary": "Get one address snapshot row",
        "tags": [
          "address-snapshot",
        ],
      },
    },
    "/api/v1/container-snapshot": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Routeware containers link to an address via \`pickup_address_id\` (and thus to a customer). Filter by \`customerId\` (joins through address), \`pickupAddressId\`, or \`containerId\`, text \`q\` on \`location_address\` or \`serial_number\`, and \`enabled\`. Pass \`cursor\` (the previous page's \`nextCursor\`) instead of \`offset\` to page deep result sets by primary-key seek instead of a scanned OFFSET.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "customerId",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "example": 345734,
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null",
              ],
            },
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "pickupAddressId",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "example": 10,
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null",
              ],
            },
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "containerId",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "example": 100,
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null",
              ],
            },
          },
          {
            "description": "Substring on location or serial (case-insensitive; maximum 100 Unicode code points)",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "q",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "description": "Substring on location or serial (case-insensitive; maximum 100 Unicode code points)",
              "example": "C-100",
              "maxLength": 100,
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "enabled",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "default": "any",
              "enum": [
                "true",
                "false",
                "any",
              ],
              "example": "true",
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "limit",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "default": 50,
              "example": 50,
              "maximum": 500,
              "minimum": 1,
              "type": "integer",
            },
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "offset",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "default": 0,
              "example": 0,
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null",
              ],
            },
          },
          {
            "description": "Last container_id from the previous page's nextCursor; takes precedence over offset",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "cursor",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "description": "Last container_id from the previous page's nextCursor; takes precedence over offset",
              "example": 99,
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null",
              ],
            },
          },
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "nextCursor": null,
                  "rows": [
                    {
                      "city": "Example City",
                      "color": "Blue",
                      "container_id": 100,
                      "container_note": null,
                      "container_type_id": 1,
                      "enabled": 1,
                      "event_code": null,
                      "frequency_ids": null,
                      "gps_locked": 0,
                      "latitude": null,
                      "location_address": "1 Main St",
                      "longitude": null,
                      "oncall": 0,
                      "pickup_address_id": 10,
                      "rfid": null,
                      "route_ids": null,
                      "serial_number": "C-100-A",
                      "service_code": null,
                      "service_code_input": null,
                      "service_code_type": null,
                      "service_date": null,
                      "state": "TX",
                      "synced_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
                      "ud_cost_share_ud": null,
                      "ud_enclosure_doors_ud": null,
                      "ud_last_compactor_inspection_ud": null,
                      "ud_last_enclosure_inspection_ud": null,
                      "ud_material_stream_ud": null,
                      "zip": "76541",
                    },
                  ],
                  "total": 1,
                },
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CustomerSnapshotList",
                },
              },
            },
            "description": "Rows and total",
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Invalid query (application/problem+json). The zod validator rejects \`q\` longer than 100 Unicode code points, an out-of-range \`limit\`/\`offset\`, or an unknown \`enabled\` value before any D1 query runs.",
          },
        },
        "summary": "List container snapshot rows (D1)",
        "tags": [
          "container-snapshot",
        ],
      },
    },
    "/api/v1/container-snapshot/export": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Streams every \`container_snapshot\` row as CSV (\`Content-Disposition: attachment\`, filename \`container-snapshot.csv\`) in \`container_id\` order. Reads in keyset pages so a full-table export never buffers the table in memory. Emits a content-hash \`ETag\`; replay it as \`If-None-Match\` for a \`304\` with an empty body. Requires \`Authorization: Bearer <CUSTOMER_SNAPSHOT_SYNC_SECRET>\`.",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "text/csv": {
                "example": "ContainerID,PickupAddressID,ContainerTypeID,SerialNumber,RFID,OnCall,EventCode,GPSLocked,Latitude,Longitude,Enabled,Address,City,State,Zip,ContainerNote,UD-Cost_Share-UD,UD-Enclosure_Doors-UD,UD-Last_Compactor_Inspection-UD,UD-Last_Enclosure_Inspection-UD,UD-Material_Stream-UD,Color,ServiceCodeType,ServiceCode_input,ServiceCode,ServiceDate,RouteIDs,FrequencyIDs,_shadow_csv_encoding,synced_at
100,10,1,C-100-A,,false,,false,,,true,1 Main St,Example City,TX,76541,,,,,,,Blue,,,,,,,1,2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z
",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
            },
            "description": "CSV download (header line plus one line per row)",
          },
          "304": {
            "description": "Not modified (If-None-Match carries the current ETag)",
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthorized",
